-- title:
--   Chart base change commutes with chart inclusions
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field with an $R$-algebra structure, and $R'$ a commutative ring sitting in a scalar tower $R \to R' \to F$, so that $F$ is an $R'$-algebra compatibly with its $R$-algebra structure. For a subset $S \subseteq F$ let `chartAlg R F S` denote the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those $x \in F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[S]$ of $F$ generated by $S$, and similarly `chartAlg R' F S` with $R$ replaced by $R'$. For $S \subseteq S'$ the map `chartIncl` is the inclusion $\mathrm{chartAlg}(R,F,S) \to \mathrm{chartAlg}(R,F,S')$ of subalgebras of $F$, and for fixed $S$ the map `chartBaseChange` is the ring homomorphism $\mathrm{chartAlg}(R,F,S) \to \mathrm{chartAlg}(R',F,S)$ given by the inclusion of these subsets of $F$. Given subsets $S \subseteq S'$ of $F$, the assertion is that the two composites $\mathrm{chartAlg}(R,F,S) \to \mathrm{chartAlg}(R',F,S')$ agree as ring homomorphisms: base changing from $R$ to $R'$ at level $S$ and then enlarging $S$ to $S'$ equals enlarging $S$ to $S'$ first and then base changing.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the chart rings of the two-chart integral model with change of base ring, in the form of a commuting square of inclusions of subrings of $F$. It is used in assembling the base-change maps on the two charts into a single morphism of the glued models, and is cited by [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_isPullback_toBase_of_isLocalization`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_isPullback_toBase_of_isLocalization) and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_iso_baseChange_baseChange_of_isLocalization`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.exists_iso_baseChange_baseChange_of_isLocalization).
-- source:
